# UBF Portal — Design System

Aesthetic: **Freshworks-inspired**. White surfaces, soft pastel accents, generous
spacing, calm hierarchy, smooth micro-interactions. Clean and quiet — never boxy or dense.

## Buttons — non-negotiable
- NEVER hand-roll an action/CTA with a raw `<button className="…">` + local CSS.
  Always: `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`.
- A raw `<button>` is acceptable ONLY for a full clickable row/card toggle, never for an action button.
- Variant = emphasis, not colour-picking:
  - Primary action on the surface → `<Button>` (default). One primary per group, max.
  - Secondary action → `variant="outline"`.
  - Low-emphasis / repeated action → `variant="ghost"`.
  - Destructive confirm → `variant="destructive"`.
  - Inline text action → `variant="link"`.
- Icon-only → `size="icon-sm"` (or `icon`) + `variant="ghost"` + an `aria-label`. Icons `lucide-react`, 16px.
- Sizes: dense rows/toolbars → `size="sm"`; default forms → default; page CTA → default or `lg`.
  Don't mix sizes inside one button group.
- Buttons are pill-shaped by design — do not override `rounded-*`.

## Tokens — use variables, never raw hex
- Surfaces: page `--color-canvas` (#F4F5F7), cards/panels `--color-surface` (#fff).
- Text: `--color-ink` (primary), `--color-muted` (secondary), `--color-faint` (hints).
- Borders: `--color-line`. Radius: `--radius`. Shadow: `--shadow`.
- Brand: `--primary` (#3B5BFE) for primary actions; `--color-accent` / `--color-accent-soft` for accent surfaces.
- Status (badges/dots): booked `--booked`, scheduled `--scheduled`, transit `--transit`, arrived `--arrived`.
- Never inline a new hex in a component. If a token is missing, add it to `:root` in `src/index.css`.

## Badges & status
- Soft pastel: tinted background (~10% of the status colour) + full-strength text.
- Use `@/components/ui/badge`; don't build pill spans by hand.

## Layout & spacing
- Cards: white surface, 1px `--color-line` border, subtle `--shadow`, `--radius`, ~16–20px padding.
- Group related controls; 8–12px gaps within a row, generous whitespace between sections.
- One clear hierarchy per screen: the primary action stands out, everything else recedes.

## Icons & type
- Icons: `lucide-react` (what the codebase actually uses in .tsx). Consistent stroke, 16px in buttons/rows.
- Type: General Sans (already global). Headings 500 weight, tight tracking. Don't set font-family in components.

## Motion
- Prefer the transitions already on the components. Add motion via Tailwind / `tw-animate-css`,
  150–200ms, ease-out. No abrupt state flips.

## Editing a screen that has hand-rolled buttons
Migrate them to `<Button>` as you touch the file. Keep existing layout wrapper classes;
only swap the button element and drop the bespoke button CSS rule it depended on.
